      "side": 1,
      "message": "Brainstorming here...\n\nGiven a class that implements `Parcelable`, we can inspect it for the `CREATOR` field, extract the object and do all of this. The problem is getting the classes that implement `Parcelable` in the BCP. In my potentially flawed understanding of Java and its lazy class loading, we only actually now details about the class once we refer to it, which makes it tricky to list all implementations of `Parcelable`. A few ideas:\n1. For all already loaded classes in the class loader (https://stackoverflow.com/a/10261850), check if it\u0027s a subclass of `Parcelable` and if so add to a list. Won\u0027t cover all, but depending on how many, should be enough, at least to get started.\n2. Get a list of parcelable implementations and hard code them here (there is one from DAC in https://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/Parcelable \"Known indirect subclasses\") into a list.\n3. Do 2, but somehow get the build system to produce this list somewhere that this test consumes such that it gets updated and the tests will always be up-to-date.\n4. Use this library (https://stackoverflow.com/a/492224) to load all subclasses of `Parcelable` (or do what it\u0027s doing).\n\nOnce we have this (potentially partial) list of `Parcelable` classes, we select one from there and test.",
